Claim_CompaniesHouseClaimer_Unit_Concrete_Test
├── when the claimer is called directly and not by delegatecall
│   └── it should revert with NotDelegateCall
├── when the namespace is empty
│   └── it should revert with EmptyNamespace
├── when the email is empty
│   └── it should revert with EmailNotNormalized
├── when the email starts with a space or a control byte
│   └── it should revert with EmailNotNormalized
├── when the email ends with a space or a control byte
│   └── it should revert with EmailNotNormalized
├── when the email has an upper case ASCII letter
│   └── it should revert with EmailNotNormalized
├── when the email has a byte that is not ASCII
│   └── it should revert with EmailNotNormalized
├── when the signer is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── when the signer is the owners sentinel
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── when the signer is Companies House
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSigner
├── when the factory deploys at another address than the derived one
│   └── it should revert with DerivedAddressMismatch
├── given the derived Safe has no code
│   ├── it should deploy it through the Safe proxy factory with the Safe L2 singleton and the 4337 module setup and the namespace and email salt
│   ├── it should swap Companies House for the signer through a v 1 approved signature
│   ├── it should emit CapxulSafeClaimed with deployed true
│   ├── it should write no storage of Companies House
│   └── it should return the Safe
├── given the derived Safe is already deployed
│   ├── it should deploy nothing
│   ├── it should swap Companies House for the signer
│   └── it should emit CapxulSafeClaimed with deployed false
├── given the Safe was already claimed
│   └── it should revert because Companies House is no longer an owner
└── when the Safe refuses the swap without reverting
    └── it should revert with SwapRefused
